      "body": "Prior harness found this PR's issue that is fixed, and this harness development found \"R11\", so I think it's already paid for itself\r\n\r\n  <details>\r\n  <summary>Concept review notes</summary>\r\n\r\n  **Diff.** Two commits.\r\n  - `294d6ffcd0` changes `TxOrphanageImpl::Erase` in about 20 lines. When the erased announcement was the\r\n  one marked for reconsideration, the mark moves to the remaining announcer with the lowest NodeId. The\r\n  comment in `AddChildrenToWorkSet` and the doc comment for `EraseForPeer` are updated, and\r\n  `txorphanage_sim` and `orphanage_tests` are updated to match.\r\n  - `345497515a` adds the `p2p_1p1c_liveness` fuzz target (547 lines, test-only).\r\n\r\n  The description matches the diff.\r\n\r\n  **Problem.** The node is sent a parent and a child (for example a CPFP), and the child does not reach the\r\n  mempool until the orphan expires or is evicted. The trigger is one announcer leaving at the wrong\r\n  moment, and an adversary can try to cause it. The evidence is a fuzzer reproduction on master. There is\r\n  no reported incident. The goal one level up is that 1p1c relay gets a child accepted in bounded time\r\n  whatever adversarial peers do.\r\n\r\n  **Baseline.** The child is delayed until orphan expiry or eviction. The attacker needs to be the randomly\r\n  chosen announcer, which is likelier with many sybil connections, and it must disconnect before its next\r\n  `ProcessMessages` turn. In that turn `ProcessOrphanTx` runs first, and the turn is skipped once\r\n  `fDisconnect` is set. If the attacker also supplies the parent and then closes the socket, the race is\r\n  plausible. The cost is delay, not loss.\r\n\r\n  **Payoff.** The fix closes the hole for both the disconnect and the eviction path. The new unit and sim\r\n  tests demonstrate it, and the liveness harness checks it end to end. The payoff is modest but real.\r\n\r\n  **Risks.**\r\n  - The invariant: \"an orphan whose inputs became available keeps a reconsiderable announcement while any\r\n  announcement exists.\" It is enforced by construction, because every removal of an announcement goes\r\n  through `Erase<Tag>`.\r\n  - The change stays inside txorphanage. net_processing and txdownloadman are untouched.\r\n  - Blast radius is relay liveness and, at worst, extra orphan-validation work. No consensus or fund \r\n  exposure, and no new Asserts.\r\n  - The change is internal and easy to reverse.\r\n  - Review cost is mostly the harness. It drives a real PeerManager, so it is a possible source of \r\n  maintenance work and flakiness.\r\n\r\n  **Prior discussion.** This came up in #31666, which introduced the single random announcer:\r\n  - sipa asked \"How is this prevented?\" \r\n  (https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/31666#discussion_r1934078679), and instagibbs laid out the\r\n  disconnect attack.\r\n  - mzumsande judged it \"really hard to pull off timing-wise\" and proposed passing outstanding workset\r\n  entries \"on to another random announcer\" at disconnect\r\n  (https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/31666#discussion_r1934886294).\r\n\r\n  That proposal was deferred, not rejected. This PR implements it, and the fuzzer reproduction is new \r\n  evidence against the impracticality point. No closed PRs attempt this fix.\r\n\r\n  **Alternatives.**\r\n  - Kept, both trades rather than improvements:\r\n    - Wtxid-keyed reconsider queue that any announcer drains. Removes per-peer ownership structurally, but \r\n  changes the TxOrphanage interface and moves the cost of other peers' work into each peer's processing \r\n  turn.\r\n    - Detect-and-heal sweep for orphans with available inputs and no reconsider mark. Catches causes not \r\n  yet known, but adds a second mechanism and CPU cost.\r\n  - Rejected:\r\n    - Mark every announcer reconsiderable. It undoes `ed24e01696` (at most one reconsiderable announcement \r\n  per wtxid) and wastes work. This is glozow's argument from #31666.\r\n    - Process one workset item at disconnect. An attacker defeats it by putting two items in the workset. \r\n  Also glozow's argument from #31666.\r\n    - Process children synchronously after the parent is accepted. It changes net_processing's per-peer\r\n  processing budget, a larger change in a costlier place.\r\n    - Docs-only or tests-only. They leave the hole open.\r\n    - Re-request the child via txrequest. Adds a new bandwidth path an attacker can trigger.\r\n\r\n  The PR takes the shallowest placement of the candidates.\r\n\r\n  **Dominance:** none.\r\n\r\n  **Verdict:** Concept ACK. The fix delivers the payoff without the harness. The harness is test-only and\r\n  has already found bugs, so splitting it out would not change the verdict.\r\n",
